# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# Snowfall with no engine: `snowfall-tile` is a 16x16 LOOP TILE whose 16 frames
# move its flakes down one pixel each (and wrap), so `fit tile` over the whole
# panel is a seamless snowfall that costs no pattern layer. The one engine is
# the drift-mode Starfield, ramped to an indigo night.
# Authored for 64x64: the top-left 32x32 is the whole scene on a small panel
# (the greeting over one tree); a 64x64 adds a second, mirrored tree further
# down the slope, its lights stepping at a different rate.
S - Silent Night
L pat 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Sky
I @pat/starfield-2d
C sliderMode 65536
R 100 0:03041a 120:1a2350 255:dfe6ff
L sprite 4 6 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Tree
I @spr/christmas-tree
L sprite 36 37 0 0 normal 100 none fill 3
N Tree 2
I @spr/christmas-tree
A 3
L sprite 0 0 64 64 normal 100 none tile 1
N Snow
I @spr/snowfall-tile
L text 0 0 0 0 normal 100 black fill 1
N Greeting
T lit MERRY CHRISTMAS
F tiny ffd166 l left 12
